{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed","id":833608,"title":"On the Anurana Becoming a Full-Fledged Changing Breed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T17:34:01-08:00","id":833608,"title":"On the Anurana Becoming a Full-Fledged Changing Breed","content":"I saw the write-up of the Anurana in the W20 Book Of The Wyrm, and I have to say I was intrigued. So, supposing that such a thing would be possible (and I refer you to the gaming rule of &quot;Why the Heck not?&quot;), how could such a transition happen, given their current status as backwoods New England frog-people like Lovecraft's nightmares after a highschool science class dissection? What sort of entity/force could become an effective patron of this new Breed? Perhaps Haha no Fukumi (The 1000 Hells, P. 60) would be a willing benefactor, having new agents to punish crimes committed with water or fire. \u200bAnyone else have any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:41:25-08:00","id":833638,"title":"","content":"I imagine some wyrm totem would probably pick them up, no need to go court a yama king from the other side of the globe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 02-19-2016, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T05:11:34-08:00","id":833782,"title":"","content":"The trouble is getting them to become a Changing Breed that's independent of the Wyrm. You'd need a spiritual patron who was sympathetic to their origins with Pentex, and wanted to pull them away from the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> It's in this light that Haha no Fukumi looks like a potential patron, being noted as a Yama King still faithful to her role under Heaven.<br /> <br /> More broadly, an entity that saw them as more than a slap in the face to Gaia...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:00:11-08:00","id":833984,"title":"","content":"Why? Saw this same suggestion done slightly differently, give the anaurana an ancient origin story, why are they the ones people feel this way on, why not the kerasi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T22:43:14-08:00","id":834275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=833984#post833984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Saw this same suggestion done slightly differently, give the anaurana an ancient origin story, why are they the ones people feel this way on, why not the kerasi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if I have to choose between featuring Deep Ones or Rocksteady in my game, I'd choose the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-21-2016, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T23:37:58-08:00","id":834292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=834275#post834275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if I have to choose between featuring Deep Ones or Rocksteady in my game, I'd choose the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>And because the Anurana's existence on the wrong side of the spiritual tracks looking to become a true Changing Breed offers up a lot of fodder for campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T08:58:08-08:00","id":834451,"title":"","content":"Where I live in Michigan there is a similar myth to the Bunyip, the First Nations people call it Mishipeshu. The story as I wrote it; after the Bunyip tribe died out, the totem Bunyip traveled the waterways out of Australia. He found his way to the America's and eventually to the Great Lakes where he got a new name by the local peoples. How his path would cross with the Anurana is simple, the eventual furniture industry and logging industry in the great lakes regions was massive and the lakes are still recovering. The automobile industry was born on the banks of the great lakes and it still has a lasting impact there. Basically the perfect breeding ground for the Anurana and the second home of a Totem the has been in hiding for the last century. <br /> <br /> Additional Reasons:<br /> He is a powerful amphibious totem, fits with the new Breed.<br /> Currently pissed at the Garou but not at Gaia.<br /> Which leads to, currently unattached to any breed.<br /> Doesn't require a lot of rework as the gift he would have access to teaching already fit the breed.<br /> <br /> General Story break down:<br /> First Act; I could easily see him guiding them from the shadows once they parted ways with Pentex much how Cockroach does with the Samsa.<br /> Second Act; Once the proved they were worth his time, he guides them to the Gurahl (also locals) to help deal with their spiritual corruption.<br /> Third Act; Confrontation with the Garou culminating in the totem making it clear they aren't going to take anything more from him, resulting in an uneasy acceptance of the Anurana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:09:47-08:00","id":834504,"title":"","content":"A changing breed for the Wyrm rather than a Mockery. Hmm.<br /> <br /> For the Wyrm following I'd likely go under the patronage of Khaaloobh, the Urge of Consumption. With their territories of toxic waste and chemical corruption they follow the Dark Fungus by distorting and polluting waters with the strange and terrifying hallucinagens their skins now produce and aid the growth and spread of their totem in the dark and damp places. They find a likeness to their incarna maejlin, the Spawn of the Wyrm as warriors for the knight of decay as they distort and disrupt the waters of the world and the minds of Gaias creatures.<br /> <br /> For the Gaia side, theres one really obvious Totemic Patron, Frog. That which represents change, the water and the Wylds wisdom and power all held within its tiny body. Proving even the greatest changes and adaptations can come from something so unexpected and versatile.<br /> <br /> These new breed protect the water ways, what they refer to as the very veins of Gaias life blood. Moving earth, summoning the rains, and guiding the rivers to keep all creatures great and small with life giving water and using their first hand knowledge of corrupt companies and poisonous proliferations of waste dumping practices to target and undo the machinations of the wyrm. One river, one lake, one water supply at time, which they guard ferociously.<br /> <br /> or something like that. If it was me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T17:50:05-08:00","id":835481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=834504#post834504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Gaia side, theres one really obvious Totemic Patron, Frog. That which represents change, the water and the Wylds wisdom and power all held within its tiny body. Proving even the greatest changes and adaptations can come from something so unexpected and versatile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the poetry of it, but has any information on Frog (or a similar spirit) ever been published?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These new breed protect the water ways, what they refer to as the very veins of Gaias life blood. Moving earth, summoning the rains, and guiding the rivers to keep all creatures great and small with life giving water and using their first hand knowledge of corrupt companies and poisonous proliferations of waste dumping practices to target and undo the machinations of the wyrm. One river, one lake, one water supply at time, which they guard ferociously. </div> </div> </div>Sort of an aquatic equivalent to the Grondr, eh?<br /> <br /> Another idea; what if they were...adopted, let's say, by the Nagah, or the Wani themselves? A young Breed that's virtually unknown (and so will be easy to cover up), based of an animal that by and large shares the same environment, and with spiritual patrons separate from the greater Umbral community","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 02-22-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T21:16:35-08:00","id":835578,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think frog has been published as a totem twice before. Once quite low (not sure if for garou or other fera without my books), but its definitely in players guide revised. <br /> <br /> If looking for a hook for adoption, I'd probably leave the nagah out of it. Due to their super secret ways, and possibly them keeping an eye on the frogs for possible assasination/judgement should they slip back to their old purposes. But go with the Mokole. They learn gifts from frog and having allies that will tend to the waters, their water holes and nesting grounds sounds like a good deal while they usher them in to the new worlds about them. <br /> <br /> Just my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T16:15:34-08:00","id":837274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=835578#post835578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably leave the nagah out of it. Due to their super secret ways, and possibly them keeping an eye on the frogs for possible assasination/judgement should they slip back to their old purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Nagahs' Great Secret hasn't kept them from participating in either the Beast Courts or the Ahadi, and keeping an eye on them for possible judgement is as good a reason to bring them in as any. Keep your enemies closer, and all that. <br /> <br /> OK, now for step two: the breeds. So far, Homid and Metis have been established. How might the frog-breed (let's call it the Anura breed) be introduced? Would it be simple breeding, or perhaps a ritual like the Corax, Camazotz, or Ratkin (they call it a plague, but I call 'em like I see 'em)? Or maybe both, with breeding being the standard for Homid and Metis, with a ritual component for elevating frog Kin to full-fledged Anura. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T16:51:03-08:00","id":837288,"title":"","content":"So, they don't know how to shift beyond Dagon, so do are you going with the idea that they gain this ability after getting a spirit sponsor? Maybe they eventually learn a gift that allows them to shift farther and then they just breed like normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T17:51:58-08:00","id":837317,"title":"","content":"I see it not so much as not knowing how, but more as not currently being capable. With a powerful enough spirit patron, the connection to proper frogs can be completed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T19:54:30-08:00","id":837370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=837317#post837317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see it not so much as not knowing how, but more as not currently being capable. With a powerful enough spirit patron, the connection to proper frogs can be completed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if that is true. Look at the Nagah and Ratkin, each has gifts which are specifically for achieving forms that other breeds have access to naturally. Obviously either way works thematically. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:45:48-08:00","id":838232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=837370#post837370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if that is true. Look at the Nagah and Ratkin, each has gifts which are specifically for achieving forms that other breeds have access to naturally. Obviously either way works thematically. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, but those are for intermediate forms, not for a base animal form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:14:58-08:00","id":844063,"title":"","content":"So, I'm putting together stats for a full-on frog form. I'm pretty much cribbing from the Ratkin rodens form, as rats and frogs can average out at about the same size (so Str -1, Dex +2, Sta +2, and Per +3). I'm also debating whether to include certain elements as Merits specific to the Breed, such as nauseating, hallucinatory, and lethal poisons of various species of frogs and toads.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any comments? Specifically, any ideas on other form abilities to include, either <i>gratis</i> or as Merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:00:48-08:00","id":844137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=844063#post844063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm putting together stats for a full-on frog form. I'm pretty much cribbing from the Ratkin rodens form, as rats and frogs can average out at about the same size (so Str -1, Dex +2, Sta +2, and Per +3). I'm also debating whether to include certain elements as Merits specific to the Breed, such as nauseating, hallucinatory, and lethal poisons of various species of frogs and toads.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any comments? Specifically, any ideas on other form abilities to include, either <i>gratis</i> or as Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>A fully aquatic form that is sort of like a mutant tadpole monstrosity might be fun, something like a <a href=\"http://scienceblogs.com/tetrapodzoology/2007/07/04/crassigyrinus-or-how-id-love-a/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Crassigyrinus</i></a>.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of the Anurana polluting families, including their own- if they were a full blown changing breed, they might have abilities, gifts or rites that allow them to taint or mark their mates or children with derangements or physical abnormalities.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:53:09-08:00","id":844160,"title":"","content":"Not really sure about the frogs getting a boost to stamina. I'm an avid herper, and amphibians tend to be more on the fragile side, no thick skin to protect them and easily effected by pollution. I know that Anurana currently thrive and require polluted water, but that's more due to the wyrm's influence. If they went Gaian I'd imagine they'd lose the requirement for toxic water and figure they'd be more aphibian like. That's just my thoughts on it though...being super hardy and amphibian to me tends to not go hand in hand. On the other hand i like the idea of them having a merits/gifts related to them gaining toxic or foul tasting skin. It could be similar to the Mokole archid trait &quot;Sickening Slime&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 03-08-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T17:31:31-08:00","id":844225,"title":"","content":"Wrote something and submitted by accident. Will update when I get it right lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T18:24:14-08:00","id":844250,"title":"","content":"Not saying anything after this point doesn't need some tweaking and review, just my thoughts.<br /> <br /> Anura Form: Strength -1, Dexterity +2 (+3 in Water), Manipulation -3, Perception +3. Can swim at 1-and-a-half speed.<br /> <br /> Amphibious: Anurana are able to hold their breath twice as long as other people can while in Homid and and Anuran and they are fully capable of breathing water as easily as air while in Anura and Dagon.<br /> <br /> Senses: Frogs have amazingly acute senses including a Jacob's Organ between their nostrils and a Lateral Line around their head, eyes, body and neck. For every form removed from Homid the Anurana may reduce the difficulty on Perception rolls by -1; Hence while in Anuran perception rolls are at -1 while in Anura they are at -3. While in Dagon or Anura their sensitivity to vibration grants them automatically benefits from the effect of the lupus Gift: Scent for Sight.<br /> <br /> Night Vision: On top of their already amazing sensory abilities, Anurana have excellent night vision and depth perception and can see in anything short of absolute darkness. In game terms this means that by spending 1 point of Gnosis they can use the dim illumination of the Umbra to make out lines in the darkness. This effect last for the duration of a scene but can be extended using gifts.<br /> <br /> Kin Species: By diversifying their animal kin, the Anurana have begun to incorporate new traits into their breed. For simplicity sake storyteller's may wish to all Anurana have similar traits regardless of their &quot;stock&quot;. Those seeking more detail may wish to assign particular advantages according to the Anurana's actual stock. Examples include:<br /> ~Flying Frogs: The webbing between the characters fingers and toes allows them to glide at a 45 degree angle from their point of take off.<br /> ~Poison Dart Frog: The character's flesh becomes incredibly toxic when enraged causing paralysis to anyone who touches or ingests it. See Mokole attribute: Contact Venom.<br /> ~Tree Frog: See Mokole attribute: Gecko Pads.<br /> ~Wood Frog: In temperatures that would freeze you to death your body shuts down. You no longer breath, your heart stops beating, your body secretes a chemical the preserves you until such time as you are able to thawed out. Once thawed, your body returns to normal function as if nothing happened.<br /> ~Casque-head Frog: As Poison Dart Frog, but your body is covered in spines that when touched, cause incredible pain for the duration instead of paralysis. During this period of time wound penalties are treated as double.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T19:06:47-08:00","id":844269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=844250#post844250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not saying anything after this point doesn't need some tweaking and review, just my thoughts.<br /> <br /> Anura Form: Strength -1, Dexterity +2 (+3 in Water), Manipulation -3, Perception +3. Can swim at 1-and-a-half speed.<br /> <br /> Amphibious: Anurana are able to hold their breath twice as long as other people can while in Homid and and Anuran and they are fully capable of breathing water as easily as air while in Anura and Dagon.<br /> <br /> Senses: Frogs have amazingly acute senses including a Jacob's Organ between their nostrils and a Lateral Line around their head, eyes, body and neck. For every form removed from Homid the Anurana may reduce the difficulty on Perception rolls by -1; Hence while in Anuran perception rolls are at -1 while in Anura they are at -3. While in Dagon or Anura their sensitivity to vibration grants them automatically benefits from the effect of the lupus Gift: Scent for Sight.<br /> <br /> Night Vision: On top of their already amazing sensory abilities, Anurana have excellent night vision and depth perception and can see in anything short of absolute darkness. In game terms this means that by spending 1 point of Gnosis they can use the dim illumination of the Umbra to make out lines in the darkness. This effect last for the duration of a scene but can be extended using gifts.<br /> <br /> Kin Species: By diversifying their animal kin, the Anurana have begun to incorporate new traits into their breed. For simplicity sake storyteller's may wish to all Anurana have similar traits regardless of their &quot;stock&quot;. Those seeking more detail may wish to assign particular advantages according to the Anurana's actual stock. Examples include:<br /> ~Flying Frogs: The webbing between the characters fingers and toes allows them to glide at a 45 degree angle from their point of take off.<br /> ~Poison Dart Frog: The character's flesh becomes incredibly toxic when enraged causing paralysis to anyone who touches or ingests it. See Mokole attribute: Contact Venom.<br /> ~Tree Frog: See Mokole attribute: Gecko Pads.<br /> ~Wood Frog: In temperatures that would freeze you to death your body shuts down. You no longer breath, your heart stops beating, your body secretes a chemical the preserves you until such time as you are able to thawed out. Once thawed, your body returns to normal function as if nothing happened.<br /> ~Casque-head Frog: As Poison Dart Frog, but your body is covered in spines that when touched, cause incredible pain for the duration instead of paralysis. During this period of time wound penalties are treated as double.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like it, my only concern there (i know this is all fun and not cannon but.....) is the use of the old &quot;Contact Venom&quot; archid trait. In my opinion it was always overpowered (paralyzed for 5 minute per point of poison not soaked, think about the implications in combat). I was personally a bigger fan of the CB20 &quot;Sickening Slime&quot;. Its not as over powered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T19:36:41-08:00","id":844282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=844269#post844269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like it, my only concern there (i know this is all fun and not cannon but.....) is the use of the old &quot;Contact Venom&quot; archid trait. In my opinion it was always overpowered (paralyzed for 5 minute per point of poison not soaked, think about the implications in combat). I was personally a bigger fan of the CB20 &quot;Sickening Slime&quot;. Its not as over powered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank You for the suggestion. I only had my Breed Books handy when I was writing that, figured its a good place to start and people can tweak as they see fit. I was pretty sure as i typed it out that one was going to be a sticking point honestly lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T20:36:25-08:00","id":844317,"title":"","content":"Honestly this thread has made me open to having them cleansed in my own game. Granted I am a fan of them as they are, they feel the most tragic. They just want to live, but are of the wyrm sue to their need for pollution. It'll be a fun moral problem for the CoG in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T00:40:31-08:00","id":844379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=844137#post844137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A fully aquatic form that is sort of like a mutant tadpole monstrosity might be fun, something like a <a href=\"http://scienceblogs.com/tetrapodzoology/2007/07/04/crassigyrinus-or-how-id-love-a/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Crassigyrinus</i></a>.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of the Anurana polluting families, including their own- if they were a full blown changing breed, they might have abilities, gifts or rites that allow them to taint or mark their mates or children with derangements or physical abnormalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am stealing both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:56:34-08:00","id":844880,"title":"","content":"Wow, loving the response this is getting!<br /> <br /> OK, to start: I'm torn between Laughing Stranger's Crassigyrinus idea and a giant frog form between Dagon and Anura. What do you think of a giant froggish form that gains a tail in the water, like the Rokea Crinos form?<br /> <br /> Next, Derzhuzad has done some great work putting together a workable Anura form, but I think the sensory effects s/he put in may be a bit much. Can we roll the difficulty drop in with the excellent night vision, but maybe drop the Scent for Sight buff and the Night Vision Gnosis expenditure?<br /> <br /> Also, CeltSPZ has contributed some excellent input on real-world frogs (kudos!). If you con think of any amphibian traits/behaviors that could make for good Gifts or be the potential basis for Rites, please don't hesitate to add them.<br /> <br /> Now, a few of my own notes: I've been thinking of including the Nagah Rage mechanics (regain one point each hour spent at least partially submerged in water, but cost twice as much in freebie and experience points to increase their rating). Any concerns?<br /> <br /> Finally, something I've been mulling over and would appreciate some input on: Rather than one Ur-Totem for the whole Breed, individual relationships are made between choruses of Anurana and individual spirits, making each chorus its own mini-tribe. Or, for a more twisted version, they learn Gifts by stalking and devouring spirits, <i>a la</i> the Maw of the Wyrm power. Heck, maybe both! Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T20:45:24-08:00","id":844890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=844880#post844880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next, Derzhuzad has done some great work putting together a workable Anura form, but I think the sensory effects s/he put in may be a bit much. Can we roll the difficulty drop in with the excellent night vision, but maybe drop the Scent for Sight buff and the Night Vision Gnosis expenditure?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do that if you like. It's just that after doing some research and taking into account that they had become full shifters; I figured that the Breed's lack of innate abilities needed to be reviewed. Their Accute Senses mechanics are taken fromthe Nagah and the Dark Sight was taken from Ratkin mechanics. Given that Frogs actually have a higher sensitivity to vibration then lizards do and they have better sight at night then rats do, I don't feel that the traits being separate abilities is really not going to far. Over all they still have less natural abilities then the other Breeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=844880#post844880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, something I've been mulling over and would appreciate some input on: Rather than one Ur-Totem for the whole Breed, individual relationships are made between choruses of Anurana and individual spirits, making each chorus its own mini-tribe. Or, for a more twisted version, they learn Gifts by stalking and devouring spirits, <i>a la</i> the Maw of the Wyrm power. Heck, maybe both! Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>A grouping of frogs is actually called an Army, amusingly, but I am assuming a Chorus is their version of a Pack? Either way I like it, they could take on different aspect of Frogs, Toads, Salamanders, Newts, Mudpuppies, and Caecilians for natural totems and then other unnatural Amphibious totems from lore. Over time psuedo-tribes could form based on Kin Species similar to the Bastet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T01:04:07-08:00","id":844969,"title":"","content":"Probably shouldn't be posting at the ass-end of the night, but...<br /> <br /> Am I the only person who finds the idea of Frog-shifters kinda... not scary or interesting? I think more of a Lovecraftian Deep One vibe is cooler and more intimidating than 'we are shifters that literally turn into frogs.' Not much creepy or threatening about Kermit. Hopping, blinking and swallowing bugs by exerting pressure with their darn eyeballs. That is what frogs can do. Compared to wolves or dinosaurs or bears or even rats, frogs seem really really underwhelming in the adversary department.<br /> <br /> Large hellbenders or even prehistoric salamanders like <a href=\"http://www.youngzine.org/article/giant-prehistoric-salamanders-found\" target=\"_blank\">Metoposaurus</a> might make for a better animal form. Alternatively, since the Anurana are unholy Wyrm-spawned monsters (despite gaining totemic legitimacy), their Lupus equivalent could be a screwed up mish-mash of amphibian beasts. It fits with their themes of pollution and corruption, as in the wild frogs are already susceptible to mutagens in their environment- and blind frog things with gills, or writhing multi-bodied caecilians would be pleasantly creepifying. <br /> <br /> Also I don't like the idea of 'Lupus' breed Anurana from a thematic standpoint- keeping them as Metis or Homid forces them to prey on kinfolk and drives them into opposition with the Garou and other Fera. If they can just spawn with the frogs and toads, it undermines what could otherwise be a visceral threat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T05:42:42-08:00","id":845033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=844969#post844969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only person who finds the idea of Frog-shifters kinda... not scary or interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bunyip, Mishipishu, The Creature from the Black Lagoon... While the image of a Battletoad makes me more long from my old Nintendo; The idea of a creature that lurks below the depths in lakes and rivers is something that I can definitely see as something that thematically could be scary.<br /> <br /> They could be interesting is that they could potentially be the spiritual successors to the Apis, if the storyteller wants to go that way. In Egyptian lore Heqet was afterall the frog goddess of fertility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:47:09-08:00","id":845074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=845033#post845033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bunyip, Mishipishu, The Creature from the Black Lagoon... While the image of a Battletoad makes me more long from my old Nintendo; The idea of a creature that lurks below the depths in lakes and rivers is something that I can definitely see as something that thematically could be scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably the Creature from the Black Lagoon with its piscine features and desire for human females seems much closer to the Deep One trope than any sort of frog prince. The Bunyip is aquatic, sure, but arguably the Bunyip is frighting as a monster because it is unknown, a mysterious, threatening Other, not because it is a creepy frog. <br /> <br /> I did forget battletoads though, so maybe you are right. That game scarred me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T08:35:23-08:00","id":845099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=845033#post845033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bunyip, Mishipishu, The Creature from the Black Lagoon... While the image of a Battletoad makes me more long from my old Nintendo; The idea of a creature that lurks below the depths in lakes and rivers is something that I can definitely see as something that thematically could be scary.<br /> <br /> They could be interesting is that they could potentially be the spiritual successors to the Apis, if the storyteller wants to go that way. In Egyptian lore Heqet was afterall the frog goddess of fertility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed with all this, for me it's not so much the animal form, but the battle form. It also occurred to me....maybe they should stick with rather common pond frogs (I.e. edible frog, bull frog ect.) Then focus on what other frogs such as dendrobates or amphibians like axolotls (gift that heightens regen? Heal agg as if it where lethal?) For gifts since they will need a slew of gifts to support them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:01:11-08:00","id":845110,"title":"","content":"Excellent points made by all. How about this: What if the Breed has a schism, with some trying to get 'legitimate' patronage from Frog, and some being backed by other, stranger things? I had an idea that, since no Triat spirits seem to want anything to do with them, what if their Deep One-like nature appealed to the Astral / High Umbral spirit representing what is arguably the most famous God-Monster in literature, Cthulhu? I know it's a bit silly, but I find there's a certain appeal to having a post-modern Totem for this post-modern Breed.<br /> <br /> Also, Laughing Stranger did make a good argument about the frog-form not being particularly frightening. CeltSPZ, you're the one of us who actually knows things about frogs. Have you heard of any naturally(!) occurring mutations that might up the creep-factor of the Anura form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 03-10-2016, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T11:34:28-08:00","id":845193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=845099#post845099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed with all this, for me it's not so much the animal form, but the battle form. It also occurred to me....maybe they should stick with rather common pond frogs (I.e. edible frog, bull frog ect.) Then focus on what other frogs such as dendrobates or amphibians like axolotls (gift that heightens regen? Heal agg as if it where lethal?) For gifts since they will need a slew of gifts to support them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that even with the Kin Species trait, its not going to remove the need for gifts. I can think of a lot of gifts the would be beneficial to them and can co exist with the trait. So say being Kin to a Dendrobate gives you 'Sickening Slime' but the spirit of that frog can also give you access to learning gifts that Paralyze or cause incredible pain like I was originally thinking. For normal Anurana they get just the normal paralysis or pain toxin from the gift and the ones that are kin to those kind of frogs get a little bonus in some way from their heritage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T14:02:11-08:00","id":845253,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with too many mutations that would really make the Anurana &quot;creepy&quot;. Most visible amphibian mutations typically involve limb defomrities (extra limbs, no limbs, underdeveloped limbs). So I had two ideas since my last post:<br /> <br /> A gift that lets you create tiny little clones of you off of pods that grow on your back. Don't have a system thought up, but its an idea based on how the Suriname toad reproduces.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2dSrUXsISA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2dSrUXsISA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2dSrUXsISA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G2dSrUXsISA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Another idea I had, if they were to go Gaian...what about some way of linking them to Srador from the W20 Umbra book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T15:54:49-08:00","id":845331,"title":"","content":"Hmm...I could see Srador taking on Anurana of such mind as his 'liegemen', or Frogs-at-Arms, but might end up starting a feud with the Bastet, or a severe dip in the local cat population.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've come to something of a stumbling block, in that I'm having trouble focusing my thoughts on these different flavors of Anurana. As such, I think we should pin down just what sort of Totem Patron they have. I've made my interest in the <b>Cthulhu</b>-esqe Totem two or three posts back; anyone want to put forth any other nominees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 03-10-2016, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:00:43-07:00","id":847436,"title":"","content":"So no-one has any opinion as to how this should proceed? OK then, I'll take that as tacit approval for the Cthulhu-Lite Totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:26:14-07:00","id":847447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=847436#post847436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no-one has any opinion as to how this should proceed? OK then, I'll take that as tacit approval for the Cthulhu-Lite Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the deep ones worship Dagon, who at one point was at war with old ones and Cthulhu. <br /> <br /> Frankly I would just leave the frogs as a mockery breed, too many changing breeds around as is imo. What next hedgehogs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T18:28:39-07:00","id":847448,"title":"","content":"What about Kelpie from the White Howlers tribe book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T21:01:22-07:00","id":847993,"title":"","content":"There's an excellent hedgehog shifter book, but I agree to a certain extent that most of the Mockery breeds should stay that. <br /> However if I were to do the Anuarana as a recovered breed first I think I'd use Kelpie from the White Howlers tribe book. Second I'd base auspices on seasons just like the Nagah and to a lesser extent Mokole. Summer would be the equivalent of Philodox Spring would be Theurge Autumn would be Galliard and Winter would be Ahroun. Or rather equivalent auspices. I would go with the Camazotz and Corax for gift inspiration as I imagine the role of messenger could be used for this breed. As for an animal equivalent go with frogs and salamanders I hesitate to add another crawlering form but in all honesty this would probably work best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T23:48:59-07:00","id":848025,"title":"","content":"If you go with Salamanders, you could use <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xolotl\" target=\"_blank\">Xolotl</a> as another totem due to his connection to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axolotl\" target=\"_blank\">axolotl</a>.<br /> While he was never a totem in the books, he can be used as inspiration.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:59:13-07:00","id":848399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=847993#post847993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if I were to do the Anuarana as a recovered breed first I think I'd use Kelpie from the White Howlers tribe book.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting suggestion; I had actually forgotten about Kelpie's existence. Its Ban easily fits with what I see the drives of 'recovered' Anurana would be, and there's a certain dramatic appeal to a diminished Incarna attempting to rebuild its power base. That said, I just can't see it happening. While individuals or given choruses of Anurana could follow Kelpie (should the Breed be inclined to/capable of Totem bonds), Kelpie represents Cunning through trickery and deception, which I don't think suits the Breed as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second I'd base auspices on seasons just like the Nagah and to a lesser extent Mokole. Summer would be the equivalent of Philodox Spring would be Theurge Autumn would be Galliard and Winter would be Ahroun. Or rather equivalent auspices. </div> </div> </div>What lead you to choosing this arrangement of Auspices?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would go with the Camazotz and Corax for gift inspiration as I imagine the role of messenger could be used for this breed. </div> </div> </div>How did you come to this idea?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for an animal equivalent go with frogs and salamanders I hesitate to add another crawlering form but in all honesty this would probably work best. </div> </div> </div>Even considering the Thousand Wing Form of the Camazotz, I think crawlerling-type forms would work best for any future insectoid/arthropod Breeds that come up; however, a swarming escape power like the Corax Gift Flight of Separation could work very well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:33:48-07:00","id":848415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=848399#post848399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An interesting suggestion; I had actually forgotten about Kelpie's existence. Its Ban easily fits with what I see the drives of 'recovered' Anurana would be, and there's a certain dramatic appeal to a diminished Incarna attempting to rebuild its power base. That said, I just can't see it happening. While individuals or given choruses of Anurana could follow Kelpie (should the Breed be inclined to/capable of Totem bonds), Kelpie represents Cunning through trickery and deception, which I don't think suits the Breed as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> What lead you to choosing this arrangement of Auspices?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'd support it because I thought we were making them more river based. River sponsors the Nagah along with Luna. So much of a Frog's life is cyclical and since so many of them have such a life cycle tied to the season I feel it goes together well. Granted I can see having Luna take them in as well due to the volume of nocturnal amphibians (but I would really advocate against Helios since Frogs don't really bask (none I'm aware of and not like lizards, turtles and crocodilians do), drying out kills them quick, and well none of the frogs don't really need UVB exposure like so many reptiles do)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T18:57:56-07:00","id":848537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=848399#post848399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting suggestion; I had actually forgotten about Kelpie's existence. Its Ban easily fits with what I see the drives of 'recovered' Anurana would be, and there's a certain dramatic appeal to a diminished Incarna attempting to rebuild its power base. That said, I just can't see it happening. While individuals or given choruses of Anurana could follow Kelpie (should the Breed be inclined to/capable of Totem bonds), Kelpie represents Cunning through trickery and deception, which I don't think suits the Breed as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think they should have many smaller totems like how the Bastet have Jamak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=848399#post848399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What lead you to choosing this arrangement of Auspices?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also came to this conclusion as the best option for there Auspices, if Auspices were to be chosen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=848399#post848399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did you come to this idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I already kind of started some gift list concepts and I used a few gifts from Corax and Camazotz, but I also used some from Rokea. I was really focusing on just a common gifts list at first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=848399#post848399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even considering the Thousand Wing Form of the Camazotz, I think crawlerling-type forms would work best for any future insectoid/arthropod Breeds that come up; however, a swarming escape power like the Corax Gift Flight of Separation could work very well...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually used Flight of Separation in my concept list, just called it Army of Frogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:26:18-07:00","id":849337,"title":"","content":"Frogs and salamanders are very tied to seasons. Messenger seems appropriate carrying the theme of river to ocean. Kelpie is a totem of cunning, and very appropriate for a redeemed breed few other totems will be willing to work with former Wyrm servants. Now if we were doing a non corrupt breed I would probably lean more towards Jamak, rather than a single totem. Again the only reason I hesitate to add a crawerling form is trampling on the insect changers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:03:41-07:00","id":850126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=849337#post849337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messenger seems appropriate carrying the theme of river to ocean.</div> </div> </div> </div>A thought occurs to me; what if, as part of accepting them as a new Breed, the Anurana are tasked with some of the duties of the Lost Breeds? The Camazotz messenger duties, the Grondr land cleansing duties )at least for rivers, lakes, ponds, and swamp lands) and the Apis eye for good breeding? These could even be tied in to the various Auspices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:26:53-07:00","id":850129,"title":"","content":"I'd stick with just one purpose. Giving them all the dead breed's duties cheapens them in my opinion. So personally I'd just keep them as the purifiers of the rivers and ponds (since they used to NEED polluted water it feels more right).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:15:36-07:00","id":850198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=845110#post845110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent points made by all. How about this: What if the Breed has a schism, with some trying to get 'legitimate' patronage from Frog, and some being backed by other, stranger things? I had an idea that, since no Triat spirits seem to want anything to do with them, what if their Deep One-like nature appealed to the Astral / High Umbral spirit representing what is arguably the most famous God-Monster in literature, Cthulhu? I know it's a bit silly, but I find there's a certain appeal to having a post-modern Totem for this post-modern Breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not at all silly. In Mage there are entire Nephandi factions which are backed by lovecraftian patrons. In Werewolf there are certain monsters - like the Inquisitors - which hint that there are evils and mysteries beyond the Wyrm.<br /> Considering the all-encompasing nature of the Wyrm, lovecraftian monsters and deities could also be part of it, or it's designs. Like an Urge Wyrm (or Majelin Incarna) being destroyed...and the replacement is an alien lovecraftian being. And then same thing happens few times more...like the nature of the Wyrm changing, or smth.<br /> (You could look up the rules of Cthulhu Wars board game for some quick run-down about the characteristics various beings from Lovecraft Mythos, and how they differ. Just be wary - it spoils reading the Mythos!)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=847447#post847447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I would just leave the frogs as a mockery breed, too many changing breeds around as is imo. What next hedgehogs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about Hedgehog Changing Breed the other day...but first one should consider Weremoles, IMO. They would of course be taking care of the undergrounds...engaged in constant warfare with the Wyrm, and stranger forces...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=847447#post847447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically the deep ones worship Dagon, who at one point was at war with old ones and Cthulhu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoiler <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-21-2016, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:18:13-07:00","id":850199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/833608-on-the-anurana-becoming-a-full-fledged-changing-breed?p=850198#post850198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoiler <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Oh please, some of us read Lovecraft before it was a trendy gamer thing to do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}